#### 📊 ParkingSpot Lifecycle States

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> FREE : spot created and added to heap
    FREE --> OCCUPIED : assign(vehicle)  synchronized
    OCCUPIED --> FREE : free()  spot re-inserted into heap
    FREE --> [*] : lot decommissioned
```

The state diagram shows the complete two-state lifecycle every `ParkingSpot` instance goes through: it enters `FREE` when `addSpot()` places it into the floor's Min-Heap, transitions to `OCCUPIED` when `assign(vehicle)` succeeds inside a `synchronized` block, and returns to `FREE` when `free()` is called on exit — at which point the spot is immediately re-inserted into the heap for the next arrival. The `synchronized` keyword on both `assign()` and `free()` is what makes this state machine thread-safe: two threads competing to take the same free spot will serialize at the monitor, so only one will see `isFree == true` and proceed. The `FREE → [*]` edge represents lot decommissioning — a rare but necessary transition that prevents the heap from holding references to removed spots.

