## 🧭 Decision Guide: When to Use K-Way Merge

| Situation | Recommendation |
|:----------|:---------------|
| Use when | K sorted lists (arrays, linked lists, files) must be combined into one sorted output, especially when K ≪ N. |
| Avoid when | Input lists are not pre-sorted (just concatenate and sort instead); or K is so large that heap overhead dominates. |
| Alternative | Two-pointer merge for K=2; `Arrays.sort` on concatenated array when N is small and code simplicity matters. |
| Edge cases | Empty lists in the input (skip them during seeding); K=1 (return the single list unchanged); duplicate values across lists (the heap handles them correctly — equal values are fine). |

