## 📖 From 3×3 Toy to OOP Interview Test

Every LLD interview question hides the same trap: the naive solution is obvious, so the interviewer immediately extends it. Tic-Tac-Toe is no different.

Naive version: a fixed 3×3 grid, two hardcoded players, if-else win check. Works in 30 lines.

Extended version: N×N board, P players with distinct symbols, swappable winning strategies (row, column, diagonal, custom), and clean state transitions. Requires deliberate OOP.

This post builds the extensible version step by step.

